	'welcome_h' => 'WELCOME ABOARD',
	'welcome_p1' => 'We believe the finest way to experience Alderwick Harbour and the Alder Hills is at your own pace, in your own time, with the people closest to you. Rather than boarding a crowded tour bus with fixed schedules, you step into a private vehicle reserved exclusively for your family.',
	'welcome_p2' => 'Your dedicated driver-guide handles the driving, navigation, parking and tolls, giving you complete freedom to explore. Whether you travel with toddlers, grandparents or luggage, your day remains quiet, comfortable and unhurried.',
	'welcome_sub' => 'A private day, drawn around one family',
	'cta_h' => 'ONE REQUEST, ONE REPLY',
	'cta_sub' => 'Tell us the dates and who is coming; the planning desk replies within 24 hours.',
	'it_h1' => 'Sample Itineraries',
	'it_lede' => 'Explore four sample journeys through the Alder Hills and Lake Morrow, designed around the pace of a single private group. Every day is redrawn for you, matching your family\'s interests, travel dates, and mobility needs.',
	'it_1_h' => 'Ridge & Harbour',
	'it_1_b' => 'This sample route begins with an 08:30 morning pickup at your accommodation before heading up into the Alder Hills. By 10:15, your private vehicle reaches a high mountain viewpoint looking out across the open valley. Descending toward the coast, you arrive at Alderwick Harbour around 12:30 for a fresh seafood lunch alongside working fishing boats. The afternoon continues at 15:00 with a gentle walk along the forested shores of Lake Morrow, where your driver-guide shares local history. The day concludes with an unhurried drop-off at your hotel door at 18:00. Like all our itineraries, the timing and stops adapt freely to your preferences.',
	'it_2_h' => 'Lakes & Cedar Shrine Path',
	'it_2_b' => 'Designed for quiet reflection and nature walks, this route connects the tranquil waters of Lake Morrow with ancient cedar groves. Departing at 08:30, your driver-guide navigates peaceful country backroads, arriving mid-morning at the moss-covered stone path of a secluded forest shrine. Even on rainy mornings, majestic trees shelter your walk before an unhurried midday meal featuring regional specialties. In the afternoon, explore lakeside viewpoints and artisan workshops nestled among the foothills. Your vehicle remains entirely yours throughout, offering a dry, warm space to rest between gentle walks before returning to your lodgings by 18:00. Every detail shifts according to weather and walking pace.',
	'it_3_h' => 'Coast & Market',
	'it_3_b' => 'Connecting coastal culture and agricultural hamlets, this journey immerses your party in regional everyday life. Starting at 09:00, drive down picturesque shoreline routes toward lively morning stalls at an outdoor coastal market, sampling regional produce and seasonal fruit alongside local growers. Midday brings dining at small harbour eateries overlooking the water in Alderwick Harbour. Later, your guide navigates winding hillsides dotted with family farms, stopping at scenic coastal pull-offs where you can photograph dramatic headlands without tour bus crowds. We adjust the pace so children and grandparents alike enjoy easy access, returning you refreshed to your hotel by 17:00 or whenever you choose.',
	'it_4_h' => 'Snow Valley Winter',
	'it_4_b' => 'During colder months, the Alder Hills transform into quiet, snow-laden landscapes. Departing at 09:00, your driver-guide maneuvers carefully along cleared valley roads in a fully winter-equipped vehicle. Mid-morning stops reveal frosted riverbanks, snow-covered forest glades, and dramatic winter vistas where hot tea awaits inside the van. Lunch takes place in a warm village dining room specializing in hearty hotpots. The afternoon offers gentle valley walks, scenic viewpoints across winter meadows, and stops at mountain lookouts before returning at 17:00 as twilight falls. The heated private cabin ensures everyone stays comfortable and relaxed regardless of outside temperatures.',
	'it_h2' => 'FOUR SAMPLE DAYS',
	'it_sub' => 'Each one is redrawn for your family',
	'fr_h1' => 'Tour Fares & Inclusions',
	'fr_lede' => 'All tours are booked exclusively for your private party and priced per vehicle rather than per person. Clear pricing ensures there are never hidden surcharges for road tolls, fuel, or parking.',
	'fr_1_h' => 'Private Vehicle Rates',
	'fr_1_b' => 'Our standard half-day tour of 5 hours for up to 6 guests is ¥48,000, ideal for city highlights or targeted visits. A comprehensive full-day tour of 10 hours for up to 6 guests is ¥82,000. For larger groups of 7 to 9 guests, we provide our spacious long van for a full-day 10-hour itinerary at ¥98,000. Point-to-point airport or station transfers are available at ¥22,000. Should your group wish to extend your day on the road, extra hours are billed at ¥8,500 per hour. For multi-day travel, our two-day itinerary is ¥172,000, which includes overnight guide lodging.',
	'fr_2_h' => 'Inclusions and Exclusions',
	'fr_2_b' => 'Every booking includes your dedicated private driver-guide, the vehicle, all fuel, road tolls, and parking fees throughout the journey. You will never encounter unexpected transport charges on the day. Guest meals, personal purchases, and admission tickets to attractions or private gardens are paid separately on-site, allowing your family complete freedom over where to dine and what to explore. For the two-day itinerary, all driver-guide lodging and accommodation expenses are fully covered within the stated ¥172,000 fare, meaning you only need to arrange your own overnight hotel reservations along the agreed route.',
	'fr_3_h' => 'Booking and Cancellation Terms',
	'fr_3_b' => 'Securing a tour is simple and risk-free. After you review and approve your personalized itinerary draft, we confirm your reservation with a 30% deposit. The remaining balance is payable prior to or on the tour date. We understand that international travel schedules can change unexpectedly, so we provide 48-hour free cancellation on all private day bookings. If your travel plans shift, simply notify our Alderwick Harbour office at least 48 hours before scheduled departure for a prompt refund of your deposit without penalties.',
	'fr_h2' => 'PRIVATE VEHICLE RATES',
	'fr_sub' => 'Per vehicle, not per person',
	'gd_h1' => 'Our Driver-Guides',
	'gd_lede' => 'Our team combines professional commercial driving with personalized regional guiding across the Alder Hills and Lake Morrow. Every guide speaks fluent English alongside additional languages to welcome international guests with ease.',
	'gd_1_h' => 'Leadership and Founding Guides',
	'gd_1_b' => 'Mika Sato-Lund founded Kuruma Tabi in 2014, directing custom itinerary planning from our Alderwick Harbour office. Mika ensures every journey balances travel times with meaningful stops. Co-founder Daniel Ferreira serves as head driver-guide, bringing extensive navigation experience and speaking Portuguese, English, and French. Daniel enjoys introducing guests to quiet coastal roads and scenic mountain overlooks far beyond standard bus routes. Together, they established our company culture: welcoming one family at a time with unhurried hospitality, absolute safety, and deep local insight.',
	'gd_2_h' => 'Lead and Regional Guides',
	'gd_2_b' => 'Amara Okafor is our lead guide, fluent in English and French, known for her warm storytelling and expertise in regional heritage around Lake Morrow. Noor Haddad brings a thoughtful approach to nature walks and architectural sights, speaking fluent English and German. Tomás Reyes guides in English, Spanish, and Japanese, expertly assisting multi-generational groups across mountain trails and harbour markets. Lin Wei-Ting provides guiding in Mandarin Chinese, English, and Japanese, specializing in coastal folklore and family-friendly dining stops. Each guide has driven regional roads for years and tailors each excursion to your preferred tempo.',
	'gd_3_h' => 'Personal Attention on the Road',
	'gd_3_b' => 'Because your guide stays exclusively with your family for the entire day, communication remains effortless from morning pickup to evening return. Guides assist with luggage handling, child safety seat installation, restaurant menu translation, and ticketing at regional sites. They continuously monitor local weather and road conditions, quietly adjusting routes if unexpected rain arrives or if your group wishes to linger longer at a picturesque spot. Their goal is not to lecture, but to provide a calm, knowledgeable presence that lets your family experience the landscape at your own natural pace.',
	'hw_h1' => 'How Planning Works',
	'hw_lede' => 'Planning a private sightseeing journey is collaborative, transparent, and built around your family. From your initial message to the day you step into the van, our five-step process ensures a seamless journey.',
	'hw_1_h' => 'Request and Draft Within 24 Hours',
	'hw_1_b' => 'The process begins when you send us your travel dates, party size, language preferences, and any particular sights or mobility requirements. Within 24 hours, our planning desk in Alderwick Harbour sends back a detailed draft itinerary. This proposal maps out realistic driving distances across the Alder Hills and Lake Morrow, suggested stops, meal venues, and scenic viewpoints. There is no automated schedule; each outline is carefully assembled by Mika Sato-Lund to ensure travel times remain comfortable for your specific group.',
	'hw_2_h' => 'Adjust, Confirm, and Deposit',
	'hw_2_b' => 'Once you review the initial proposal, we refine the stops, timing, and activities together. You can swap a mountain hike for an artisan visit or schedule extra downtime for young children. When you are completely satisfied with the itinerary, you confirm the reservation with a 30% deposit. Our 48-hour free cancellation policy gives you flexibility should flight arrangements or holiday schedules change. With your vehicle and driver-guide locked in, you can look forward to your journey with total peace of mind.',
	'hw_3_h' => 'Your Day on the Road',
	'hw_3_b' => 'On the morning of your tour, your private driver-guide greets you directly at your hotel lobby or station platform at your requested departure time. The day unfolds at your preferred rhythm: linger over coffee at Alderwick Harbour, take extra photographs at high mountain viewpoints, or pause for spontaneous rest stops. Because tolls, fuel, and parking are all pre-paid, you never have to worry about transport logistics. At the end of the journey, your guide drops you off safely at your accommodation.',
