	'hw_s5_p' => 'The day',
	'hw_h2' => 'THREE STAGES',
	'hw_sub' => 'From first message to the morning pickup',
	'vh_h1' => 'Private Vehicle Fleet',
	'vh_lede' => 'Travel in private, climate-controlled comfort designed specifically for family groups and small parties. Our fleet is maintained to commercial standards and equipped for safety across all seasons in the Alder Hills.',
	'vh_1_h' => 'Minivan and Long Van Capacities',
	'vh_1_b' => 'We operate two distinct vehicle configurations tailored to your party size. Our comfortable standard minivan seats up to 6 guests with generous legroom and panoramic windows, ideal for couples, small families, and groups exploring narrow country lanes. For larger parties or extended family groups of 7 to 9 guests, our long van provides spacious seating and expansive headroom without sacrificing ride quality. Both vehicle types are reserved entirely for your private use, ensuring a quiet, relaxing environment without strangers sharing your cabin.',
	'vh_2_h' => 'Luggage, Child Seats, and Accessibility',
	'vh_2_b' => 'Traveling with multiple generations requires practical vehicle amenities. Our vans feature generous rear cargo bays capable of accommodating full-sized suitcases, folding strollers, and travel equipment with ease. We provide clean, certified child safety seats and booster cushions fitted securely before arrival at no extra charge. Low-step entry thresholds, wide-opening sliding doors, and sturdy assist handles make boarding easy for elderly travelers. Our vehicles accommodate folding wheelchairs, ensuring guests of all mobility levels can reach scenic viewpoints across Lake Morrow and the hills in total comfort.',
	'vh_3_h' => 'All-Season Road Safety',
	'vh_3_b' => 'Navigating mountain passes and coastal curves requires meticulous vehicle upkeep and seasonal preparation. Our vehicles undergo strict commercial mechanical inspections and are maintained in peak condition at our Alderwick Harbour base. During winter months in the Alder Hills, vans are equipped with dedicated winter tires and cold-weather equipment. On-board amenities include multi-zone climate control, privacy glass, mobile device charging ports, and bottled water. Your driver-guide handles all navigation, parking, and traffic conditions, leaving you free to enjoy the countryside views.',
	'vh_h2' => 'THE FLEET',
	'vh_sub' => 'Two vans, one family at a time',
	'ab_h1' => 'About Kuruma Tabi',
	'ab_lede' => 'Founded in 2014 in Alderwick Harbour, Kuruma Tabi was established to give overseas travelers an unhurried, private way to experience the Alder Hills and Lake Morrow.',
	'ab_1_h' => 'Our Founding Story',
	'ab_1_b' => 'Kuruma Tabi was founded in 2014 by Mika Sato-Lund and Daniel Ferreira at 12 Quay Road in Alderwick Harbour. Having observed how rigid tour bus timetables rushed international visitors through fragile landscapes, they envisioned a more personal alternative: dedicating one private vehicle and one experienced driver-guide to a single family for the entire day. Daniel took the wheel as head driver-guide, bringing Portuguese, English, and French fluency, while Mika led itinerary curation. Over the past decade, that founding principle has guided every mile traveled across our coastal and mountain routes.',
	'ab_2_h' => 'Our Operating Values',
	'ab_2_b' => 'We believe that the best journeys respect both the visitor and the destination. We never herd large tour groups, visit commercial commission souvenir stores, or force guests into rushed itineraries. Instead, our team focuses on private flexibility, allowing families to discover quiet cedar trails, scenic roadside viewpoints, and authentic harbour dining. By employing multilingual guides who speak English, French, German, Spanish, Japanese, and Mandarin Chinese, we bridge local culture with international hospitality. We treat every excursion as a dedicated partnership, planning carefully around your interests and physical comfort.',
	'ab_3_h' => 'Rooted in Alderwick Harbour',
	'ab_3_b' => 'Our headquarters at 12 Quay Road remains the active center of our daily operations. From our harbour base, our office team monitors road conditions, coordinates seasonal itineraries, and answers itinerary requests six days a week. We maintain close working ties with local farmers, independent restaurant owners, and coastal fishermen across the Alder Hills and Lake Morrow. These regional relationships allow us to introduce our guests to genuine local life, whether that means recommending a seasonal harbour lunch or showing you a quiet forest shrine path away from crowds.',
	'ab_h2' => 'OUR STORY',
	'ab_h3' => 'HARBOUR BASE',
	'ab_sub' => 'Founded in 2014 at 12 Quay Road',
	'ab_k' => 'How we work',
	'rq2_h1' => 'Request an Itinerary',
	'rq2_lede' => 'Begin planning your private chauffeured tour by sending us your travel details. Our planning desk reviews every inquiry individually and responds with a customized itinerary draft within 24 hours.',
	'rq2_1_h' => 'How to Submit Your Request',
	'rq2_1_b' => 'To start, submit our online inquiry form or write directly to our planning desk at plan@kurumatabi.example. Please share your prospective travel dates, the size of your group, any child seat or accessibility needs, preferred languages, and sights you hope to visit around the Alder Hills and Lake Morrow. Whether you require a standard 5-hour half day, a 10-hour full day, an airport transfer, or a multi-day journey, we build your day from scratch. There is no obligation when requesting a proposal.',
	'rq2_2_h' => 'Office Hours and Response Time',
	'rq2_2_b' => 'Our operations office at 12 Quay Road in Alderwick Harbour is open Monday through Saturday from 09:00 to 18:00. We reply to all itinerary inquiries and emails within 24 hours. Our private tours operate daily from 07:00 to 21:00, allowing early morning departures for sunrise mountain viewpoints or evening returns after sunset dinners. If you have an urgent inquiry outside office hours, our on-duty coordinator reviews incoming correspondence to assist traveling families promptly.',
	'rq2_3_h' => 'Deposit and Free Cancellation',
	'rq2_3_b' => 'Once you review and approve your proposed day plan, your vehicle and driver-guide are reserved upon receipt of a 30% deposit. The remaining balance is payable prior to or on the date of your tour. We recognize that travel schedules can shift, which is why we provide a 48-hour free cancellation policy on all private day tours. If you need to cancel or adjust dates, simply notify us at least 48 hours before your scheduled pickup for a full refund of your deposit.',
	'rq2_label' => 'REPLY',
