	'rq2_tab' => 'Write to us',
	'qa_h1' => 'Frequently Asked Questions',
	'qa_lede' => 'Find clear answers to common questions regarding private vehicle bookings, fares, guide languages, and day-of-tour logistics across the Alder Hills and Lake Morrow.',
	'qa_1_h' => 'How many guests can travel in a private vehicle?',
	'qa_1_b' => 'Our standard minivan accommodates up to 6 guests comfortably, which is perfect for couples, families, and small parties traveling with luggage. For larger family groups or friends traveling together, our long van accommodates between 7 and 9 guests. Every tour is strictly private; your vehicle is reserved exclusively for your party, and you will never share the cabin or guide with outside guests.',
	'qa_2_h' => 'What is included in the tour fare?',
	'qa_2_b' => 'All published fares are charged per vehicle, not per person, and cover your dedicated driver-guide, the vehicle, fuel, highway road tolls, and parking fees throughout the journey. There are never surprise transport surcharges. Personal expenses such as meals, entrance tickets to private facilities or museums, and personal shopping are paid directly by guests on the day. For two-day itineraries, guide lodging expenses are also fully covered within the ¥172,000 package fare.',
	'qa_3_h' => 'What is your cancellation policy?',
	'qa_3_b' => 'We offer free cancellation up to 48 hours before your scheduled tour departure. If your flight is delayed or your vacation plans change, inform us at least 48 hours in advance, and your 30% deposit will be promptly refunded in full without cancellation fees. Cancellations made within 48 hours of departure may forfeit the deposit to compensate for vehicle and driver scheduling.',
	'qa_4_h' => 'What languages do your driver-guides speak?',
	'qa_4_b' => 'All our driver-guides speak fluent English. In addition, our team offers guiding in French, German, Spanish, Japanese, and Mandarin Chinese. Mika Sato-Lund coordinates planning, head guide Daniel Ferreira speaks Portuguese, English, and French, Amara Okafor speaks English and French, Noor Haddad speaks English and German, Tomás Reyes speaks English, Spanish, and Japanese, and Lin Wei-Ting speaks Mandarin Chinese, English, and Japanese. Please let us know your preferred language when requesting your itinerary.',
	'qa_5_h' => 'Can the itinerary be changed during the day?',
	'qa_5_b' => 'Yes. Because your vehicle and driver-guide are reserved exclusively for your family, the schedule is completely flexible. If you wish to spend extra time at a picturesque mountain overlook, take a relaxed walk by Lake Morrow, or stop early for lunch at Alderwick Harbour, your guide will adapt the route. If weather conditions change, such as rain over the ridges, your guide can immediately suggest sheltered alternative stops like the cedar shrine path.',
	'qa_6_h' => 'Do you provide child safety seats and assist guests with limited mobility?',
	'qa_6_b' => 'Yes. We provide clean, certified child seats and booster seats tailored to your children\'s ages free of charge, properly installed prior to pickup. For elderly guests or travelers with limited mobility, our vehicles feature low entry steps, wide sliding doors, and sturdy assist handles. We also accommodate folding wheelchairs in the luggage compartment and regularly design gentle, step-free itineraries, such as scenic viewpoints and flat harbour walkways, ensuring all generations travel comfortably.',
	'qa_h2' => 'EVERYDAY QUESTIONS',
	'qa_sub' => 'Seats, fares, languages and the day itself',
	'nl2_h1' => 'Season Notes Newsletter',
	'nl2_lede' => 'Subscribe to Season Notes for early access to seasonal tour schedules, blooming forecasts, winter driving windows, and quiet travel routes across the Alder Hills.',
	'nl2_1_h' => 'Early Access to Seasonal Bookings',
	'nl2_1_b' => 'Peak travel periods in the Alder Hills and Lake Morrow—including vibrant autumn foliage and the crisp winter snow season—often book out months in advance due to our private, one-vehicle-per-family policy. Subscribers to Season Notes receive priority notification whenever seasonal reservations open, giving your family the first choice of dates and multilingual guides. We also share specialized notices regarding road conditions and seasonal route adjustments before public announcements.',
	'nl2_2_h' => 'Notes from the Road and Regional Insights',
	'nl2_2_b' => 'Written directly by our guides and founders in Alderwick Harbour, Season Notes delivers concise quarterly dispatches on regional life. Learn about emerging farm-to-table lunch spots, quiet cedar walking trails, local seasonal produce markets, and coastal viewpoints that offer shelter on misty days. We share genuine observations gathered from our daily driving routes, offering practical inspiration for overseas visitors planning private travel through our region.',
	'nl2_3_h' => 'Respectful Correspondence',
	'nl2_3_b' => 'We respect your inbox and send only four to six thoughtful bulletins per year. We never share subscriber contact details, sell data to third parties, or send promotional spam. Each issue includes a simple one-click unsubscribe link. Enter your address and send the request; once it reaches us we add you to the seasonal dispatch, so you can plan your next private journey through the Alder Hills at your own pace.',
	'nl2_h2' => 'JOIN THE LIST',
	'nl2_sub2' => 'Your address, nothing else',
	'th_h1' => 'Thank you',
	'th_lede' => 'Thank you for writing to Kuruma Tabi. If your request reached us, the planning desk replies within 24 hours.',
	'th_p' => 'While you wait, look through the sample days or the fares. Nothing is booked until you approve a draft and pay the 30% deposit, and you can cancel free up to 48 hours before departure.',
